> I've played a few spell casting valkyries.  They have to be
> very high level before they get powerful at attack spells but
> with a lot of extra effort they can be quite effective at it.
> By the very late game the pattern to use on advancing monsters
> can be cast, zap, fire all before melee.

Agreed.  If nothing else, I like to get cure sickness at 0%
failure rate before the planes (and Valks can do this).  But
magic missle, cone of cold, etc., are a great alternative to
slinging daggers as well.

In the other direction, all of the decent armor you're likely to
find at the beginning hinders spell-casting considerably.  Which
means that even a Wizard will likely spend a good deal of time
slinging daggers before he starts depending on spells.

